  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, $f(x)=x^{13}+x^{11}+x^{9}+x^{7}+x^{5}+x^{3}+x+19$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{r}\r\n\\Rightarrow f^{\\prime}(x)=13 x^{12}+11 x^{10}+9 x^{4} \\\\\r\n+7 x^{6}+5 x^{4}+3 x^{2}+1\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\n$f^{\\prime}(x)$ has no real root.\r\n$\\therefore f(x)=0$ has not more than one real root.",
